{"id":"bf5133176eaa12c8","group":"92","path":"92/92-thm-completeness-fo.md","title":"Completeness of First-Order Logic","display":"thm-completeness-fo — Completeness of First-Order Logic","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Gödel's Incompleteness Theorems","book_abbrev":"92","label":"92-thm-completeness-fo","aliases":["92-thm-completeness-fo"],"display":"thm-completeness-fo — Completeness of First-Order Logic","depends_on":["[[92-df-logical-consequence]]","[[92-df-provable]]","[[92-df-signature]]","[[92-df-logical-axiom]]","[[92-ax-modus-ponens]]","[[92-ax-generalization]]","[[92-lem-soundness-fo]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Gödel's Incompleteness Theorems"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"92"},{"key":"label","html":"92-thm-completeness-fo"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>92-thm-completeness-fo</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-completeness-fo — Completeness of First-Order Logic"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"c75bb5270ee96d5a\" href=\"?note=c75bb5270ee96d5a\" title=\"92-df-logical-consequence\">92-df-logical-consequence</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"51c43e0240787ebb\" href=\"?note=51c43e0240787ebb\" title=\"92-df-provable\">92-df-provable</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"d666a3e3ee6c8148\" href=\"?note=d666a3e3ee6c8148\" title=\"92-df-signature\">92-df-signature</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"e948c25f4a467fa1\" href=\"?note=e948c25f4a467fa1\" title=\"92-df-logical-axiom\">92-df-logical-axiom</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"16613851c4bce386\" href=\"?note=16613851c4bce386\" title=\"92-ax-modus-ponens\">92-ax-modus-ponens</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"906680bfce5f44c0\" href=\"?note=906680bfce5f44c0\" title=\"92-ax-generalization\">92-ax-generalization</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"29a0403e0c65ae9d\" href=\"?note=29a0403e0c65ae9d\" title=\"92-lem-soundness-fo\">92-lem-soundness-fo</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Phi\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_G\">\\(\\Phi\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_G\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Sent}_G\">\\(\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Sent}_G\\)</span> (premise set and conclusion)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{LogAx}_G\">\\(\\mathrm{LogAx}_G\\)</span> (logical axioms, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"e948c25f4a467fa1\" href=\"?note=e948c25f4a467fa1\" title=\"92-df-logical-axiom\">92-df-logical-axiom</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MP},\\mathrm{Gen}\">\\(\\mathrm{MP},\\mathrm{Gen}\\)</span> (the fixed Hilbert rules, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"16613851c4bce386\" href=\"?note=16613851c4bce386\" title=\"92-ax-modus-ponens\">92-ax-modus-ponens</a> and <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-10\" data-note=\"906680bfce5f44c0\" href=\"?note=906680bfce5f44c0\" title=\"92-ax-generalization\">92-ax-generalization</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal F_\\Phi\">\\(\\mathcal F_\\Phi\\)</span> (definition target for the same premise calculus as in <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-11\" data-note=\"29a0403e0c65ae9d\" href=\"?note=29a0403e0c65ae9d\" title=\"92-lem-soundness-fo\">92-lem-soundness-fo</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}completeness\\text{-}fo} \\vdash\n\\mathcal F_\\Phi\\coloneqq(\\Sigma_G,\\mathrm{LogAx}_G\\cup\\Phi,\\mathrm{MP}\\cup\\mathrm{Gen}),\n\\qquad\n\\Phi\\models_G\\varphi\\Longrightarrow\\mathcal F_\\Phi\\vdash\\varphi\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}completeness\\text{-}fo} \\vdash\n\\mathcal F_\\Phi\\coloneqq(\\Sigma_G,\\mathrm{LogAx}_G\\cup\\Phi,\\mathrm{MP}\\cup\\mathrm{Gen}),\n\\qquad\n\\Phi\\models_G\\varphi\\Longrightarrow\\mathcal F_\\Phi\\vdash\\varphi\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>关键符号：</p>\n<ul>\n<li>一阶逻辑完备性定理（Gödel 1930）</li>\n<li>与<a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-12\" data-note=\"29a0403e0c65ae9d\" href=\"?note=29a0403e0c65ae9d\" title=\"92-lem-soundness-fo\">92-lem-soundness-fo</a>合并可得<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Phi\\models_G\\varphi\\Longleftrightarrow\\mathcal F_\\Phi\\vdash\\varphi\">\\(\\Phi\\models_G\\varphi\\Longleftrightarrow\\mathcal F_\\Phi\\vdash\\varphi\\)</span>；两边现已使用同一签名和同一明确演算</li>\n<li>这与不完备性定理的区别：\n<ul>\n<li>完备性定理：关于逻辑系统本身</li>\n<li>不完备性定理：关于算术公理系统</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>完备性定理保证逻辑推导&quot;足够强&quot;</li>\n<li>不完备性定理：算术公理系统&quot;有缺口&quot;</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"92-df-logical-consequence","status":"resolved","id":"c75bb5270ee96d5a","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[92-df-logical-consequence]]","embed":false},{"target":"92-df-provable","status":"resolved","id":"51c43e0240787ebb","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[92-df-provable]]","embed":false},{"target":"92-df-signature","status":"resolved","id":"d666a3e3ee6c8148","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[92-df-signature]]","embed":false},{"target":"92-df-logical-axiom","status":"resolved","id":"e948c25f4a467fa1","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[92-df-logical-axiom]]","embed":fa